            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Title\u202fIII directs that evidence derived from a wiretap order must be suppressed when there is an error in obtaining, issuing, or executing that order."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c1e50778fe2020797859a3344348f89f5516d580f24e1d7710bf06265ae3f6ab",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c1e50778fe20-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner argues that a facially insufficient order makes any communications intercepted pursuant to that order unlawfully obtained and therefore subject to suppression."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c1e50778fe2020797859a3344348f89f5516d580f24e1d7710bf06265ae3f6ab",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c1e50778fe20-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States, the government maintains that the orders were not insufficient on their face because they were merely overbroad."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c1e50778fe2020797859a3344348f89f5516d580f24e1d7710bf06265ae3f6ab",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c1e50778fe20-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked whether there was an invalid application of the order, noting that the only intercepts introduced were from the District of Kansas."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c1e50778fe2020797859a3344348f89f5516d580f24e1d7710bf06265ae3f6ab",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c1e50778fe20-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer expressed concern about the need for the order to specify authority to wiretap both in Kansas and elsewhere."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c1e50778fe2020797859a3344348f89f5516d580f24e1d7710bf06265ae3f6ab",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c1e50778fe20-0002-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 50,
              "start": 50
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked about the circuit split on the issue, indicating uncertainty about how lower courts have resolved the question."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c1e50778fe2020797859a3344348f89f5516d580f24e1d7710bf06265ae3f6ab",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c1e50778fe20-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 61,
              "start": 61
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy inquired whether the government had used intercepts from other states, underscoring the scope of the alleged overreach."
      }
    ],
